Dear Joaquin,

no, you don't fill in the 0 at the right place in the vector of inits. You must provide the inits in exactly the same order as the coefficients are ordered in the model. The coefficient for y2.perch in the submodel for colonization comes after the colonization intercept. Therefore, you must provide the starting values in this order (note the filled in 0 in red).

starts <-c(1.16699470,4.13455875,0.53512199,-1.28441477,  0, 0.18498429,-0.03367617)

Then, you do

model.2 <- colext(psiformula = ~y1.seed+y1.perch, # First-year occupancy
                  gammaformula = ~y2.perch , # Colonization
                  epsilonformula = ~ 1, # Extinction
                  pformula = ~ 1, # Detection

                  data = umf1, starts = starts)

Best regards  --- Marc

